  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) achieves 0.4224 acc, only marginally above RNA-only config_011 (0.4106 acc), while image-only config_017 is far weaker (0.2266). This suggests the image modality contributes very little, possibly because the weighted fusion strategy is not effectively leveraging it. Question: Does changing fusion from weighted to concat (the only difference in config_006) meaningfully alter the multimodal gain over RNA-only? Why this experiment: It is a clean single-variable comparison against our best result, isolating the fusion mechanism. If concat yields a substantially different result, we learn that fusion strategy is a key lever and should be prioritized in all future multimodal runs. If it is similar, we can rule out fusion as the bottleneck and redirect effort toward RNA encoder choice, image encoder, or multiprofile aggregation. Under a limited budget, resolving this binary question with one experiment is the most efficient use of the next slot."
}

